    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The JSON routing overlay in SPEC_METHOD.md's urn:stdo:bounded-context:product-definition-routing maps identity, location, relations and discovery without owning referenced meaning. One definition is published per distinct current Product WHAT, conventionally stdo_<label>.json or stdo_default.json for one definition. Definition Label is a stable lowercase ASCII letter/digit/hyphen/underscore discovery label unique only in its directory. product.definition_id is a stable URI for one continuing mutable WHAT line, unique in the discovered workspace set, not immutable Product identity. Definition root is the containing directory; relative references resolve against the file's retrieval URI, while product.source_project may locate that root or elsewhere.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 398,
          "quote": "The suffix `<label>` is the **Definition Label**: a stable lowercase local\ndiscovery label made from ASCII letters, digits, hyphens, or underscores. It is\nunique only among definitions in the same directory. It is not Product\nidentity. The `product.definition_id` URI inside the definition is the\n**Product-Definition Identity**: the stable identity of the mutable\nproduct-definition line, unique within the discovered workspace definition\nset. It identifies one continuing `WHAT` definition, not one immutable released\nProduct.",
