    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The pair (immutable stdo://releases/<cut>/ URI, installed-manifest SHA-256). The deterministic manifest binds annotated tag object, commit, repository tree, standards subtree, exact standards inventory/member bytes and admitted auxiliary payloads; it is transport/integrity evidence rather than replacement constitution.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 515,
          "quote": "(immutable stdo://releases/<cut>/ URI, installed-manifest SHA-256)\n```\n\nThe URI identifies one immutable annotated RC cut. The digest identifies the\ndeterministic installed-release manifest that binds its tag object, commit,\nrepository tree, standards subtree, exact standards inventory, member bytes,\nand admitted auxiliary payloads. The manifest shape is owned by\n`schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json`. It is transport and integrity\nevidence, not a replacement constitution.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSTDO%20Product%20Definition%20Overlay%20And%20Layout%20Independence%2FShared%20Installed%20Release%20Basis%20And%20Toolchain%20Manager",
          "start_line": 507
