      "key": "coverage_completeness_boundary",
      "statement": "Self-inspection of a finite inventory cannot establish universal absence of undiscovered material evaluations without an independently established closed-domain completeness predicate. Formal incompleteness motivates caution but does not prove this particular set incomplete. Coverage remains falsifiable and externally challengeable by outside human knowledge, independent review, historical failures/predecessors, mutation/adversarial/counterexample search, live operation/user behavior, adjacent workspace/domain comparison, and changes in actors, law, dependencies or topology. An explicit residual boundary is required; metaphysical or universal completeness is not.",
