      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1093,
          "quote": "The following observations trigger frame diagnosis:\n\n- a competent actor repeatedly cannot see a known material violation;\n- a local repair creates or duplicates another authority path;\n- work repeatedly resets after apparently valid local completion;\n- long implementation loops produce no stable closure;\n- proof passes while the claimed outcome remains unbound;\n- a material failure is visible only after broad integration;\n- reviewers repeatedly expand context without reaching a decidable question;\n- two actors use the same frame name but evaluate different material relations;\n  or\n- a topology mutation leaves prior verdicts apparently current.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#Reference%20Frame%20Method%2FDiscovery%20And%20Revision%2FMissing-Frame%20Signals",
          "start_line": 1082
        }
      ],
      "key": "missing_frame_diagnosis_triggers",
      "statement": "Diagnosis is triggered by repeated competent-actor blindness to a known material violation; repair creating/duplicating authority paths; repeated resets after apparently valid completion; long loops without stable closure; passing proof with an unbound outcome; failure visible only after broad integration; repeated context expansion without a decidable question; same frame name used for different material relations; or topology mutation leaving verdicts apparently current. These are diagnostic triggers, not proof that a new frame is required.",
