      ],
      "key": "drift_example_contract",
      "statement": "The example attends to mutable Source Project → checkpoint → Release Cut → Product, installed Development Product → authorized builder substrate, and authoring Product → directed dependency contract → dependent Product. All Product/Install/checkpoint/contract/actor/grant/evidence coordinates compare by declared identity and exact digest; source/target roles are not interchangeable. Builder differs from authored Product; scenarios/specializations require Product re-entry to become new Products; affected edges keep owner/contract; mutable state cannot replace immutable review subject. Sources are the example goals, product-definition, requirements, composition-contract and candidate-delta URIs. Summaries, generated maps, precedent, matching output, shared actors, nesting and tool reachability are excluded as Product/composition authority. The reviewer has Product/identity/composition/source-acquisition/counterexample capabilities and an evaluation grant; operation authority is none; semantic authority stays with cited owners and decision/acceptance/publication with Product/release owners. Evidence comprises exact authority sources, candidate bytes/delta, dependency identities, contracts, affected-path observations and counterexamples. Independently reacquire every authority/candidate/dependency/contract through the cited route/grant and retain identities, digests, acquisition time and failures. Depend on exact preservation results for every affected Product and one result per affected directed edge; return one closed result to urn:example:conjunction:product-change:7. Every listed material change reopens affected reliance, preserving historical subject/basis and requiring RF-005 applicability for reuse. Uninterpretable basis gives invalid_basis; missing scope gives out_of_frame; undecidable stale/unresolved support gives indeterminate unless other evidence decides. Meaning change requires owner re-entry.",
      "uncertainty": "Illustrative URIs do not supply actual underlying subjects, grants or evidence; RF-005 is not included."
    },
    {
