      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": ["The product-local cut name may also be the Git tag name in a qualifying single-project source."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 65,
          "quote": "In a release source carrying one independently released project, that name may\nalso be the Git tag name. In a shared release source it is the suffix of the\nproject-qualified Git ref defined below. Equal product-local cut names do not\ncollapse releases owned by different projects.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/RELEASE_METHOD.md#Release%20Method%2FPosition",
          "start_line": 62
        },
        {
          "end_line": 82,
          "quote": "Release handling is downstream of intake triage. A bug, feature, regression,\nor release blocker first receives its change class, lawful re-entry point,\naffected scope, downstream proof obligations, and version-line disposition.\nThe existence of an RC window does not authorize untriaged mutation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/RELEASE_METHOD.md#Release%20Method%2FPosition",
