      "statement": "Only owner declaration of stable identity/owner/basis/scope establishes context; consuming standards need explicit owner relation to define concepts there. Resolve in order: occurrence scope/nearest explicit context; exact basis/applicable authorities; admitted local definitions/imports; all applicable owner overrides/disambiguations; admit exactly one remaining concept. Equal spelling/case/shape/location/nesting/actor/implementation proves no meaning/identity/equivalence/inheritance/authority, and different spelling proves no inequality; use semantic address or authorized relation. Filenames/headings/index/schema/bare URI/prompt/proximity never accidentally declare contexts. Zero applicable concepts is unresolved, multiple ambiguous; withhold material use without familiar/frequent/recent/nominal/glossary fallback. Exact-one predicate: established uniqueness=satisfied; complete applicable set with zero/multiple=falsified; incomplete search/unavailable definition=indeterminate, not proved zero; invalid/contradictory address/basis=invalid_basis; outside scope/capability=out_of_frame. Keep diagnostic and no conventional default. GLOSSARY_GUIDE is non-deciding locator to owning declarations, cannot define/repair context or establish shared meaning; applicability requires selected owning clause or explicit target import.",
